#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525080} :activity/id #uuid "9264b1c1-1f4d-5132-9bcf-b88ec17fcbba" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049288 :topic/id #uuid "ea0735e9-7712-5a1c-a626-25cab33f54cb" :topic/math-academy-id 6386} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525075 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "075ff70c-8adb-53e9-8868-dac30ec95b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524395} {:answer/id #uuid "11f6e6ae-3c6c-50c6-99cc-458271767c9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524412} {:answer/id #uuid "a69c5953-f455-53cf-a745-4db7c010554c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524646} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf1af4e-c02d-5acb-a898-ed1acac8e812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524755} :answer-field/id #uuid "65f9587c-2102-51c3-9018-cf73e669ee77" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2b8556-b100-5f8e-bc9f-9cd87c21cb7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524513} {:answer/id #uuid "72385776-67d2-5118-b12a-b9ffbb9a1976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{18\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524565} {:answer/id #uuid "92909ea3-1683-5e8f-b3a3-8b2af56ef7af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524612} {:answer/id #uuid "e88ad1ac-4369-5a83-8114-9aecaa890952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{54\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524791}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524612} :answer-field/id #uuid "b41532f6-c5f8-55db-9dde-0e3b62dd91b0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1741c2e1-8000-5ded-a8b9-94a357d2c64a" :question/math-academy-id "q-343887" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=f(x),$ where the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}={{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $4$-periodic function $(L=2)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFor $n=3$, we have ${\\omega }_{3}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ Since ${\\omega }_{3}=\\omega ,$ the $n=3$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=3$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{3}(x)=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{3}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}))+x(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{3\\pi }{2}B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″} & =-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{3}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}):$\n\n$$\n[-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}{y}_{{p}_{3}}]+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}{y}_{{p}_{3}}=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3\\pi A=0 \\\\ 3\\pi B=\\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}A=0 \\\\ B=\\frac{1}{27\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=\\frac{x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "195b0b09-5636-555a-9d5e-886ade5b2b0a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525085}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525080 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317447 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27e72c91-6260-57d4-8f2b-d360cd74d1b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi (36-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315345} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0f4d4a-2783-5d38-996e-52ca4cc7173c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi (36-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316256} {:answer/id #uuid "e004ee5f-c254-5252-8869-1073aea1cb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi (36-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316361} {:answer/id #uuid "fe8de36c-f73d-5178-bafa-3d6b6a68abaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi (36-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316543}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316256} :answer-field/id #uuid "d50cf4cc-94a7-5eeb-8680-cbc2d70101de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3d266502-5760-5926-ac9e-cf2e92540f0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-343875" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}+9y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the free term and all the cosine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+9({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms to find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(9-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\frac{36-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{b}_{n}(36-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}{4}=\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi (36-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi (36-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1f09e7df-3236-5077-9169-9cb1ad13c54e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525093}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525085 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397701 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60cf0d89-49e8-5b67-80c1-e7d2d7a3ffb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{8\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397703} {:answer/id #uuid "a1876296-7211-55be-aba4-bfdcc1a01df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{16\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397704} {:answer/id #uuid "09aff7b4-dbdd-58ab-8229-b25ef4b4ba18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397705} {:answer/id #uuid "fe23c02e-5cbf-556d-b7f3-55b796e71bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{8\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397706}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397706} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef63660a-274c-5dd7-9740-8afb5e0d6094" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397702} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b222e16-92bf-5e7b-a075-99b8093081a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397708} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cd2371-beae-59d9-8d7e-94aae5b22c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397709} {:answer/id #uuid "964c305f-0261-5625-959d-d4db38c740ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397710} {:answer/id #uuid "63032ea2-0b98-59b3-8f8b-f8122510525d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397711}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397710} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f3873a4-d6a5-52d5-8df1-9961c00d5836" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dd94ef93-5daf-566f-92be-7aef938749ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-343899" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x),$ where the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}={{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}=\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $4$-periodic function $(L=2)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFor $n=2$, we have ${\\omega }_{2}=\\pi .$ Since ${\\omega }_{2}=\\omega ,$ the $n=2$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=2$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{2}(x)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{2}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))+x(-\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{2}}^{″} & =-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{2}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{2}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{2}}]+{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2\\pi A &=0 \\\\ 2\\pi B &=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A &=0 \\\\ B &=\\frac{1}{8\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}=\\frac{x}{8\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3917470a-f482-5821-99c5-2f8790e885a5"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525093 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e4cc218-73fe-5998-8ccf-bc16f3b90e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524514} {:answer/id #uuid "b9355ba0-889c-5450-99e3-818ab0a4f2f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524676} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a1ae82-6bda-5f83-b1fc-96118fbd6f97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524728} {:answer/id #uuid "e570c1cd-6353-5178-af72-bcd3aab8e4d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524783}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524514} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f9455a9-07ca-5997-b4ca-16fa2b6ab07c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35c42206-68dd-51fc-99b6-ae210d259dac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524482} {:answer/id #uuid "3b2f4c1a-00a1-55c0-9e44-6bcc54f3f7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524488} {:answer/id #uuid "8c0a8364-45bf-574e-bb9d-0ac0a859448d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524603} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0bdb29-be00-5a7a-ae5b-f5917ddd3a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524725}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524482} :answer-field/id #uuid "e37207bf-0563-5832-ad30-c6a23c3c930c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9b306e59-ac03-5a23-8563-3ae450882f03" :question/math-academy-id "q-343882" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-5y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that all the cosine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})-5(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))=5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n-5\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})=5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and sine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=5 \\\\ {b}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-5)=\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-1 \\\\ {b}_{n}=-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "52d5eeed-9b84-5f58-91ed-53e58dd47c9d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525122}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525122 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "344d0e42-cd70-5ad8-90fc-7db764816086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524478} {:answer/id #uuid "86854eda-5a8f-50ea-94b0-dd55b64266ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524590} {:answer/id #uuid "ce713a1f-b2ec-53d9-97c8-17515419704d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524724} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1a145b-0c0c-558c-963e-71228c0de2a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524800}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524590} :answer-field/id #uuid "04a2bae6-aeac-5a01-8bbe-2da7affb6702" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e74e00-5bf0-5bcb-9c73-5ac12785eb89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524390} {:answer/id #uuid "20391762-3990-5977-9275-05105acc9764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524440} {:answer/id #uuid "96006c5e-26f2-501a-82c3-1c733fab3f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524620} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2ce446-0043-5cc6-9d9f-038477aa3b6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524662}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524662} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b8556e9-1a54-5d0b-a5a5-5efa77eeb553" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "234b7e73-d01a-5fb8-b7f2-7b7733987672" :question/math-academy-id "q-343886" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-10y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼10+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that all the cosine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})-10(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))=10+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n-10\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-10)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})=10+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and sine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-10\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=10 \\\\ {b}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-10)=\\frac{5(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-1 \\\\ {b}_{n}=\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a80e8457-da19-59dc-ac4a-260518248f13" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525075}}] :activity/title "Solving ODEs Using Fourier Series" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524369}]}
